    "summary_one_sentence": "To rescue his failing country club and gain his father's long-sought approval, a failed tennis pro breaks a deeply personal vow by taking up pickleball.",
    "summary_short": "A washed-up tennis professional finds himself at a desperate crossroads when the country club he loves faces impending financial ruin. In a bid to save the business and finally earn the respect of his demanding father, he must face his pride head-on. To achieve his goals, he is forced to break a sacred vow and cross over into the wildly popular world of pickleball. This unexpected journey tests his values, his relationships, and his definition of success.",
    "summary_long": "The Dink follows a fallen tennis prodigy whose career ended in disappointment, leaving him struggling to find purpose and connection. His life takes a critical turn when the local country club, a bedrock of his family's heritage and his own identity, falls into severe financial trouble. Desperate to prevent its foreclosure and win over his stern, traditionalist father who has always viewed him as a failure, the former pro searches for any viable solution. He realizes that the club's survival hinges on embracing the booming, yet fiercely mocked, sport of pickleball. Doing so requires him to shatter a personal oath he swore years ago to never pick up a paddle. As he begrudgingly enters the competitive pickleball circuit, he confronts intense rivalries, unusual team dynamics, and his own elitist snobbery. Along the way, the quirky world of pickleball forces him to rediscover his love for athletic camaraderie and re-evaluate his toxic relationship with his father. Through comedic mishaps and high-stakes matches, he learns to embrace humility, unity, and a new kind of redemption.",
